# mcp-parallel-factor-published - the runner hands every child it execs the
# contention factor, so a child can widen a deadline it enforces itself.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-fixit-plugin-concurrency-is-pinned-to-a-ci-constant AC-1, the
# producer half. (*Runner).parallelFactorEnv (internal/test/runner/runner_exec_util.go)
# renders the entry and runner_exec.go puts it in the environment of every
# `cmd=` process. Nothing else in the harness crosses that boundary, so an entry
# dropped from that list is invisible to every Go test in the runner package.
#
# The VALUE is deliberately not pinned: it is 1 when this file runs alone and
# ParallelTimeoutHeadroom when it runs inside a parallel suite, and a test whose
# expected value changes with the way it is run cannot assert one. What is
# asserted is that the variable REACHES the child at all -- printenv exits 1 and
# prints nothing when the name is unset, so removing the entry turns this test
# red without any value to agree on.
#
# The consumer half, that cmdMcp multiplies its deadline by the value, is
# mcp-ready-under-load.ci and TestMCPReadinessScalesWithConcurrency.
#
# PREVENTS: the MCP readiness deadline silently falling back to the authored
# value on every host, which is the fixed-10s defect this spec exists to close.

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=printenv ze.test.parallel-factor:timeout=15s
expect=exit:code=0
# (?m) is load-bearing: the runner matches the regex against the whole captured
# stdout, trailing newline included, and Go anchors ^ and $ to the text without
# it.
expect=stdout:pattern=(?m)^[0-9]+$
